### US-001: Define and enforce UI action parity across mobile and desktop
Status: in_progress
Depends on: None

Description:
As a user, I want the same-named buttons on mobile and desktop to perform the same actions so the UI is predictable.

Acceptance Criteria:
- [ ] Create an action-parity map (document or config) listing each shared action name and its expected behavior
- [ ] Update mobile and desktop UI labels and handlers to match the action-parity map
- [ ] Example: a button labeled 'Disconnect' removes the active session but keeps the pairing on both platforms
- [ ] Negative case: a mismatched label/action is detected (manual QA checklist) and corrected before release


